course: dictionary
lesson: 7454
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one the writer means. The word «poor» is a good example. Read the clues before you choose a meaning.
explain: «In the old days poor children were taught to call richer people sir.» Richer is set against poor, so poor means having little money. In «Side vision is good at spotting movement but poor at seeing detail», the word «but» shows a contrast, so poor means not skilled at something.
explain: Poor can also show feelings. «Poor puppy, it is cold» means we feel sorry for the puppy, not that the puppy has no money. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Poor has several meanings: having little money, not good enough, feeling sorry for someone, and not skilled at something.
fact: Poor can also be a noun: the poor means poor people as a group.
fact: Poor changes form: poorer means more poor, and poorest means the most poor.
fact: In science, a poor conductor lets little heat or electricity through.
fact: Common phrases include poor health, poor eyesight, poor weather, a poor mark and poor thing.
exercise: «In the old days poor children were taught to call richer people sir.» What does poor mean here? | Not skilled at a task | Feeling sorry for someone | *Having little money and few things | Not good enough in quality
exercise: «Side vision is good at spotting movement but poor at seeing detail.» What does poor mean here? | Having very little money | *Not skilled at something | Very old | Feeling sorry for someone
exercise: «Poor puppy, it is cold.» Which feeling does poor show? | *Sorry for someone | Bored by something | Angry at someone | Proud of someone
test: «Poor weather kept us indoors all day.» What does poor mean here? | Having little money | *Bad, not good enough | Feeling sorry for someone | Skilled at something
test: In «the rich and the poor», what does poor mean? | Not skilled at something | A poor mark at school | Feeling sorry for someone | *Poor people as a group
exam: In «a poor conductor of heat», poor means: | Very old | Feeling sorry for someone | Having little money | *Weak, letting little heat through
